    "day_shift_interpretation": "For LEAR, shift=-1 feeding features from a day later is expected to *improve* MAE, not degrade it: the shifted price_lag_24h column then holds the target day's own price. That is the measurement of what the leak would be worth, and the reason degrades_for_every_shift is False here where C3's naive floor had it True \u2014 the naive model reads only price_lag_168h, which any whole-day shift breaks in both directions. What the probe establishes is that the harness is sensitive to time; the gate-closure guard, not the sign of this number, is what refuses the leak on the real matrix.",
